.TH "PB-CONFIG-STATUS-BAR" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-config-status-bar - Configure the interactive terminal status bar


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb config status-bar [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Configure the interactive terminal status bar

.PP
Inspect, set, preview, or reset local status-bar preferences. These settings affect interactive terminal display and do not modify remote shell state.

.PP
Configuration commands distinguish local CLI settings from synchronized repository content. Inspect current state before changing it; synchronization reports conflicts instead of silently overwriting one side. The --json option provides structured output for scripts where supported.

.PP
With --json, this command group lists its available commands.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for status-bar


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-config(1)\fP, \fBpb-config-status-bar-preview(1)\fP, \fBpb-config-status-bar-reset(1)\fP, \fBpb-config-status-bar-set(1)\fP, \fBpb-config-status-bar-show(1)\fP
